            "start": 57.0
          },
          {
            "id": 76.0,
            "kind": "region",
            "len": 10.0,
            "start": 185.0
          }
        ],
        "expanded_text": "In a matter of days, the campaign at the Barwyn, held by the Free Cities ground toward what the dispatches would call a mixed result \u2014 a conclusion that satisfied no one completely. At the Barwyn, the terms of a mixed result were ratified under a sky that offered no comment. The people who had lived through the campaign signed where they were told to sign. The generation that came after accepted a mixed result as inheritance \u2014 the debts and the gains both, without the memory of choosing either.",
        "fragment": 364.0,
        "fragment_ids": [
          364.0,
          372.0,
          378.0
        ],
        "id": 0.0,
        "mentions": [
