          ]
        },
        "significance": 0.0,
        "start_tick": 30.0,
        "text": "In the Barwyn, where Marrow had once walked with authority, a quieter era of diminishment began. Marrow name still appeared in the registries, but it carried a different weight now. Children of the household were raised on stories of what had been, and the silence of what was."
      },
      {
        "category": 20.0,
        "cluster_type": 3.0,
        "end_tick": 80.0,
        "expanded_mentions": [
          {
            "id": 4.0,
            "kind": "faction",
            "len": 15.0,
            "start": 5.0
          },
          {
            "id": 76.0,
            "kind": "region",
            "len": 10.0,
            "start": 37.0
          },
          {
            "id": 76.0,
            "kind": "region",
            "len": 10.0,
            "start": 200.0
          },
          {
            "id": 76.0,
            "kind": "region",
            "len": 10.0,
            "start": 428.0
          }
        ],
        "expanded_text": "What the Free Cities accomplished in the Barwyn during this period was less a conquest than a reorganization \u2014 the same territory, different loyalties, different logic. The transition of authority in the Barwyn was conducted, by the standards of such things, with restraint. Old obligations were discharged; new ones were incurred. The exchange was transactional in form, if not always in spirit. Whether the new arrangement in the Barwyn was better than the one it replaced depended, as such judgments usually do, entirely on where one had stood in the arrangement it replaced.",
        "fragment": 307.0,
        "fragment_ids": [
          307.0,
          312.0,
          318.0
        ],
        "id": 4.0,
        "mentions": [
