            "start": 149.0
          },
          {
            "id": 64.0,
            "kind": "region",
            "len": 11.0,
            "start": 398.0
          }
        ],
        "expanded_text": "A generation passed before the people of the Rasvane allowed themselves the word they had long been avoiding. In a matter of days, the population of the Rasvane contracted \u2014 not through catastrophe but through the quiet arithmetic of departures exceeding arrivals, births failing to replace deaths, and a general sense that the future lay elsewhere. Later administrations would attempt revivals of the Rasvane \u2014 some earnest, some merely rhetorical. None recovered what the long erosion had taken, because erosion does not leave the original shape intact beneath its work.",
